  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I had made a request here a while ago for decoupled headlook (like onward). Just wanted to let you guys know that there is an app that let's you do this now with VRchat actually.\n\nIf you download \"natural locomotion\" from steam there is a VRchat profile. You can set decoupled headlook in there before launching the game. This will allow you to traverse forward while being able to look around. It's the \"controller relative\" setting under VRchat profile.\n\nYou don't even have to use the arm swinging walk with the app, it's optional (I play seated in VR)\n\nHave fun, and hopefully the devs can maybe implement this someday. I love it!",
